  "notes": "SEMESTER CHANGE: on 5 Aug 2025 the Saudi Cabinet approved a return from three terms to TWO semesters starting 1447 AH (2025/26), keeping 180+ school days (al-Watan: https://www.alwatan.com.sa/article/1168211). Science books are now in two parts. Grades 2,3,5,6,8,9: term 1 = units 1-3 (chapters 1-6), term 2 = units 4-6 (chapters 7-12). Grade 1: term 1 = chapters 1-5, term 2 = chapters 6-10. Grade 7: term 1 = chapters 1-6, term 2 = chapters 7-13. EDITIONS: today is Oct 2026, which is school year 1448. Term-1 entries use the 1448 books where they are posted (grades 1-7 and 9). Grade 8 term 1 and all term-2 entries use 1447, because the 1448 term-2 books are not out yet. The 1448 term-1 books for grades 1,2,3,5,6,7,9 match 1447. ONE REAL CHANGE: in grade 4 term 1, unit 3 is now «صحة الإنسان» (chapter 4 الأمراض والعدوى: الأمراض، العدوى وانتقالها; chapter 5 التغذية والصحة: المحافظة على الصحة، الغذاء والتغذية). It replaces «الأرض ومواردها» (المعادن والصخور، الماء), which moved to term 2 as unit 4 (chapter 6). The grade-4 term-2 page found (labelled 1447) already uses this new numbering, chapters 6-10. Some sites (e.g., beadaya file/206 and file/3090) still show the older grade-4 layout. GRADE 9: some sites (beadaya file/433, almrj3) put the term-1 units in a jumbled order. The order used here comes from salisedu: term 1 = طبيعة العلم وتغيرات الأرض + أسس الحياة + كيمياء المادة; term 2 = الروابط والتفاعلات + الحركة والقوة + الكهرباء والمغناطيسية. It gives balanced chapters 1-6 / 7-12, and the 1447 term-2 book confirms it. CONFIDENCE: unit and lesson titles are confirmed from two independent Saudi book-solution sites (beadaya.com, salisedu.com), which reproduce each book's table of contents; I could not open the official ien.edu.sa platform directly. Lesson titles were taken verbatim from those sites, with spelling normalized. The book's side features (التركيز على المهارات، أعمل كالعلماء، قراءة علمية، كتابة علمية، العلوم والرياضيات، أتهيأ للقراءة) were left out because they are not lessons. CONCEPTS: all grades are marked concepts_inferred=true. The concept lists were written from the vocabulary (المفردات) of the Saudi adapted McGraw-Hill series, matched to the confirmed lesson titles, using Saudi terms (المخلوقات الحية، البناء الضوئي، الدائرة الكهربائية…). They were cross-checked against a grade-9 glossary on beadaya, key terms from the grade-4 health lessons (haqibati.net), and some lesson question headings. Each lesson has 4-8 concepts. The grade 1-2 concepts are the least certain, because those books have little formal vocabulary. Islamic studies content was excluded entirely. Totals: 18 grade-term entries, 225 lessons, 1,479 concept mentions, 894 unique concept names (many repeat across grades, e.g., دورة الماء، الدائرة الكهربائية)."
